      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(external): support macOS desktop credentials",
        "body": "Replaces https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/pull/976 after its stack base merged into main.\n\n## Summary\n\n- allow the generic `external` provider to preserve Linux, macOS, native Windows, and WSL2 targets, including ARM64 hosts\n- persist target and Windows-mode routing so later lease commands restore the captured platform without overriding explicit target flags\n- add source-bound external desktop credentials via username plus password environment-variable name\n- use provider credentials consistently for WebVNC, screenshots, input, native VNC handoff, daemon children, and routed leases\n- authenticate macOS ARD or legacy VNC locally, then expose an already-authenticated RFB stream without sending the desktop password to the coordinator\n- add authenticated `webvnc --preflight`, including RFB 3.3, 3.7, 3.8, and accepted alias-banner handling\n- validate native-Windows work roots against drive roots, user profiles, protected directories, traversal/ambiguous components, short names, ADS, and reserved device aliases\n- document macOS credentials, native-Windows work-root requirements, preflight, and routing behavior\n\n## Maintainer hardening\n\n- merged current `main` and resolved the WebVNC/RFB stack against the one-time portal handoff architecture\n- preserved legacy Parallels password-only VNC while using ARD accounts for provider-supplied macOS credentials\n- kept registered static macOS endpoints host-managed and preserved two macOS WebVNC slots for controller plus observer\n- made a configured-but-missing desktop password environment variable fail closed instead of falling back to an unrelated remote password file\n- scrubbed desktop credentials from every unrelated provider, adapter, SSH, shell, and controller child while keeping the one credential-owning daemon on stdin only\n- made persisted credential routes fail closed on malformed state, symlinks/reparse points, insecure ownership or permissions, and same-path replacement; generated children are bound to the exact route digest and cleanup to a unique generation\n- preserved explicit, persisted, and server-labelled work roots even when they equal another platform's default\n- made server-authenticated macOS portal viewers credential-free, with clean ACL-controlled share URLs and correct RFB 3.7 `None` negotiation\n- made foreground SSH tunnel cleanup terminate and verify the full ProxyCommand process tree, including when the SSH leader already exited\n- made canceled controller children wait for verified process-group exit before removing their durable recovery handle\n- resolved registered macOS desktop credentials before scrubbing the daemon environment and forwarded them only through the one-shot supervisor stdin gate\n- kept `webvnc status` usable without loading desktop secrets\n- added a changelog entry thanking @MuduiClaw\n\n## Verification\n\nExact head: `75b64da67dbfa9c276e52fbceebbdbfc4188e424`\n\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go test -race ./...`\n- `scripts/check-go-coverage.sh 90.0` — core coverage 90.3%\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh` — 54 command docs, 74 providers, 214 Markdown files, docs-site build\n- `scripts/test-provider-lifecycles.sh`\n- `scripts/test-go-modules.sh`\n- `go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode@v0.45.0 -test ./...`\n- Linux, Windows, and Darwin `internal/cli` test-binary cross-compiles\n- Worker format, lint, typecheck, 937 passed/3 skipped tests, and Wrangler dry-run builds\n- branch-wide AutoReview after integrating current `main` found and fixed the registered auto-WebVNC credential handoff; the focused repair review and second full branch review both completed with no accepted/actionable findings\n- exact-head externally orchestrated Crabbox Linux validation via `blacksmith-testbox` lease `tbx_01kx505602cdnhnea53qsxs6z7` — the remote command asserted `git rev-parse HEAD` equals `75b64da67dbfa9c276e52fbceebbdbfc4188e424`, completed with exit 0, stopped the one-shot lease, and confirmed no residual inventory ([delegated run](https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/actions/runs/29066317178); its Testbox step is expectedly canceled during Crabbox-owned teardown)\n- exact-head hosted CI: 12/12 checks passed — [CI](https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/actions/runs/29066136355), [connector smokes](https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/actions/runs/29066136339)\n- credential-free process matrix at `b31436b21c189c08b0dba7561a0025294a9ca988` exercised Linux, macOS, native Windows, and WSL2 through the real CLI with local provider/SSH shims\n  - persisted routing reused after config removal\n  - hostile provider labels overwritten by trusted routing\n  - POSIX, encoded PowerShell, and WSL2 command forms verified\n  - macOS VNC output redacted; adapter environment isolated\n  - all claims, routing, and synthetic provider resources removed\n\nThat process matrix remains supporting runtime proof. The current head integrates current `main`, adds the registered auto-WebVNC credential regression, and has fresh full Go race, Worker, script, docs, branch-review, hosted-CI, and exact-head Blacksmith Linux proof. Real External macOS Screen Sharing remains credential-bound: no approved test endpoint currently exposes both SSH and Screen Sharing with a task-scoped credential. No endpoint security settings were changed. Retain that provider-backed live-proof decision gate until such an endpoint is available or maintainers explicitly waive it.\n\n## Security and configuration\n\nThe desktop password value is never stored in Crabbox config, routing state, argv, or portal handoff. Config and daemon routing carry only the environment-variable name. The Crabbox process reads the value when an authenticated desktop operation starts, preserves it as opaque data, and fails closed if the configured variable is absent or empty.\n\nFor macOS WebVNC, Crabbox authenticates to ARD/VNC locally and gives the browser/coordinator only an already-authenticated RFB stream. Repository config cannot redirect an inherited desktop credential reference without a matching trusted or explicit override.\n",
